---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Stamp from '../components/Stamp.astro';
---

<Base title="Glider logic" description="A working NOT gate built from glider collisions in Conway's Game of Life, and why that makes Life a universal computer.">
  <section class="logic" data-logic>
    <header class="section-head section-head--page">
      <p class="kicker mono" data-decode>instrument · signals &amp; gates</p>
      <h1 class="section-head__title">Glider <em>logic</em></h1>
      <p class="section-head__lede">
        Two glider guns, one crossing, no wires. A missing glider is a 0, a present one is a 1, and a collision is a computation.
      </p>
      <Stamp id="P" />
    </header>

    <div class="logic__grid">
      <div class="logic__stage">
        <canvas class="logic__board" data-logic-board aria-label="The NOT gate running in Conway's Life"></canvas>
        <div class="lab__transport mono">
          <button type="button" class="button button--sm" data-logic-play>▶ run</button>
          <button type="button" data-logic-reset>reset</button>
          <label class="lab__speed">speed <input type="range" min="5" max="120" value="30" data-logic-speed /></label>
          <span class="lab__readout">gen <b data-logic-gen>0</b></span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="logic__panel sheet torn">
        <form class="logic__form" data-logic-form>
          <label class="mono" for="logic-bits">input bits</label>
          <div class="lab__row">
            <input id="logic-bits" class="mono lab__code" data-logic-bits value="10110010" maxlength="32" pattern="[01]*" spellcheck="false" />
            <button class="chip">send ↵</button>
          </div>
        </form>
        <button type="button" class="chip logic__switch" data-logic-switch aria-pressed="true">input switch: 1</button>
        <p class="mono logic__queue">queued: <span data-logic-queue>empty</span></p>
        <div class="logic__tapes mono">
          <p><span>in</span><output data-logic-in>·</output></p>
          <p><span>¬in</span><output data-logic-out>·</output></p>
        </div>
        <p class="logic__lamp mono"><i data-logic-lamp aria-hidden="true"></i> output glider</p>
        <p class="lab__note">
          Gun A fires the input stream (acid). Gun B, its mirror image, fires a clock stream (violet) every 30 generations. At the
          crossing each A-glider annihilates its B partner completely. Delete an A-glider at the input tap and its partner flies
          through: the output is <b>NOT</b> the input, five periods (150 generations) later.
        </p>
      </aside>
    </div>

    <article class="unveiled__chapter">
      <p class="unveiled__num mono">why it matters</p>
      <div class="unveiled__text">
        <p>
          A NOT gate plus a way to merge two streams (a second collision that kills a clock glider if <i>either</i> input is
          present) gives NOR, and NOR alone builds every Boolean circuit. Add memory from glider loops or stable blocks, and the
          board holds a computer. Berlekamp, Conway and Guy sketched this in <i>Winning Ways</i> (1982); Paul Rendell built a
          working Turing machine in Life in 2000. The same story plays out in one dimension: Matthew Cook's proof that
          <a href="/posts/rule-137/">Rule 110</a> is universal uses gliders colliding against a periodic background.
        </p>
        <p>
          The complexity stamp says <b>P</b> because evaluating a Boolean circuit is P-complete: this gate is the unit of that
          problem. The board it runs on is not so tame. Ask what a large Life pattern will eventually do and you are asking what a
          computer will eventually do. That question lives in <a href="/archive/#RE">RE</a>.
        </p>
        <p class="mono logic__provenance">
          Geometry found by exhaustive search and checked on random bit strings: scripts/find-not-gate.mts,
          scripts/verify-not-gate.mts.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>
  <script>
    import { mountLogic } from '../lib/logic';
    document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', mountLogic);
  </script>
</Base>
